## Scope: Documents Management Core

**In scope for Core:**
- Metadata search (patient name, document type, source, department, date, urgency)
- Filter and sort by any metadata field
- Practice tag taxonomy with role-based creation and deletion (admin only creates/renames/deletes; all users apply)
- Tag deletion: confirmation warning required; cascade removal from all documents and dependent Smart Views on confirmation
- Unique tag enforcement (duplicate names blocked)
- Searchable and sortable tag taxonomy list (A-Z / Z-A)
- Starter tag set provided at setup
- Inline tag application on document rows
- System-generated Smart Views in sidebar (no manual Smart View creation)
- Drag-to-Smart-View gesture applies tag; workflow state preserved
- Organisation-scoped tag taxonomy (tags isolated per organisation; not shared across organisations)
- Configurable tag cap per organisation (default 50, range 1–200) with warning at 80% of configured maximum
- Unused tag flagging at 90 days (Should Have)
- Bulk Code action within Smart Views (eligible documents: patient-matched)

**Explicitly not in scope — in-document content search (rich text / OCR search):**
> Search within document body content is out of scope for Phase 1. This requires OCR or AI processing capability not available in this phase. Deferred to Phase 2 pending OCR/AI pipeline availability.

**Explicitly not in scope — custom user-created folders:**
> User-created arbitrary folders (DocMan model) are not implemented. The folder-like experience is delivered by Smart Views. Workflow-state queues (Inbox, Filing Queue, Coding Queue, Tasks) are system-defined and not editable by users.

**Out of scope for Documents Management Core — Parking Lot:**

> Full-text corpus search across all document body content is **not required in the 30-day Documents Management Core phase**.
> This capability requires server-side search infrastructure (e.g. Amazon OpenSearch). At EMIS Web install base scale this represents a meaningful ongoing infrastructure cost (estimated £300–3,000+/month depending on rollout scale and OCR requirements). Architecture and cost decisions must be confirmed before this can be progressed.
>
> **Parking lot:** Full corpus full-text search — potential future phase. Entry condition: infrastructure cost agreed; search architecture confirmed with engineering team.

> AI tag suggestions (using OCR-derived metadata via the REQ-012 pipeline) are **not in scope for Documents Management Core**. The tag model and data structures defined in this requirement are designed to accommodate suggestions in a future phase without architectural rework.
>
> **Parking lot:** AI tag suggestions — future phase. Entry condition: REQ-012 OCR/AI pipeline live in production; HAZ-DOC-026 mitigation (explicit user confirmation) confirmed in V1e clinical safety review; SaMD boundary assessment confirms tag suggestions remain below medical device classification threshold.

