## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — search queries returning patient-linked documents must be audited
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — each bulk file and bulk code event creates an individual audit entry per document per REQ-009 before patient record is written
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — the Tags model must visibly preserve workflow state so users can confirm documents have been actioned; the UI must never imply that tagging constitutes actioning
- **CLIN-009:** Clinical Safety Logging — bulk actions logged with user ERN; patient identifiers recorded as ERNs not NHS numbers
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — search returning no results must be clearly distinguished from a search that failed; empty state must never mask an error; partial bulk action failures must not be swallowed silently

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-019:** User assumes no results means a document does not exist — action taken on incorrect assumption that a document is absent
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Medium

- **HAZ-DOC-020:** Search returns documents from outside the user's authorised scope (e.g. wrong practice)
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-025:** User believes tagging a document constitutes actioning it — document remains unprocessed in workflow queue
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium (behaviour change from folder-based model)
  - **Risk Level:** High
  - **Note:** This hazard is specific to the Tags model. Mitigated by always displaying the workflow state alongside tags in the UI, and by ensuring Smart Views show the workflow queue column.

- **HAZ-DOC-026:** AI-suggested tag applied without user confirmation — incorrect tag leads to missed routing or incorrect workload division
  - **Severity:** Low (tags are organisational only; clinical actions require separate steps)
  - **Likelihood:** Low (tags are suggestions requiring confirmation)
  - **Risk Level:** Low

- **HAZ-DOC-030:** Bulk code action applies incorrect SNOMED code(s) to multiple patient records simultaneously — erroneous code committed to many patients in a single action; clinical harm multiplied across patient population
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Low (mandatory confirmation step with code preview and patient list before execution)
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-031:** Partial bulk action failure occurs silently — some documents in the batch fail to file or code; user believes all succeeded; unprocessed documents remain invisible as incomplete
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-018:** Empty search results clearly labelled with the query that was run; error states visually distinct from genuine empty results
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-019:** All search and filter queries scoped to the authenticated user's practice context; cross-practice results not possible
  - **Type:** Business Logic + Auth
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-024:** Document workflow state (Inbox / Filing Queue / Coding Queue / Done) always displayed in the document list alongside tags. Tag application never changes workflow state. UI does not present tags as a proxy for completion status.
  - **Type:** UI Control + Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete — workflow state is server-enforced; tags are additive metadata only

- **MIT-DOC-025:** *(Future phase — deferred)* AI tag suggestions to be displayed as visually distinct pending chips requiring explicit user confirmation before applying. Retained for design reference when AI suggestions are introduced.

- **MIT-DOC-030:** Confirmation step before bulk code execution displays: (a) total number of patient records to be coded, (b) named list of patients whose records will be updated, (c) the exact SNOMED code(s) to be applied. User must explicitly confirm; confirmation cannot be bypassed.
  - **Type:** UI Control + Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete (substantially reduces risk; residual risk is deliberate user error)

- **MIT-DOC-031:** Per-document outcome reported after every bulk action: each document individually marked as succeeded or failed with the specific error reason; user prompted to retry or manually action each failed document; no silent failures permitted.
  - **Type:** Business Logic + UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

