## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-001:** Data Minimisation — search results return only the triage metadata fields (as per REQ-001); full document content not returned in search results list
- **IG-002:** Privacy by Design — search index does not expose patient data beyond what the authenticated user is authorised to access
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — Article 6(1)(e) public task + Article 9(2)(h) health data
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — search index (if server-side) encrypted at rest

### Data Handling
- Metadata search index contains only the defined triage metadata fields; no clinical content in the index for V1
- In-document search operates client-side on the already-loaded document rendition; no additional data transmitted
- **Tags** are practice-level organisational metadata, not patient clinical data. Tag names must not contain patient-identifiable information (enforced via validation on tag creation).
- **Smart Views** are saved filter configurations; they store filter criteria only, not document content or patient data
- Tag taxonomy and Smart View definitions stored server-side, scoped to the practice
- AI tag suggestions derived from OCR metadata via the same pipeline as REQ-012; same IG controls apply

### GDPR Articles
- **Article 5(1)(c):** Data minimisation — search results limited to authorised, necessary fields
- **Article 9(2)(h):** Special category health data — appropriate access controls on search scope

