## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance

### Product KPIs
- Metadata search latency (query submitted → results returned)
- Search result relevance (user selects first result vs. refines query — proxy for relevance quality)
- Filter/sort usage patterns (which fields used most — informs future UX improvements)
- Tag application rate (manual vs. drag-to-Smart-View — measures feature adoption)
- Smart View usage rate (system-generated tag views)
- Tag taxonomy size per practice (monitors proliferation)
- Bulk action usage rate (proportion of filing/coding sessions using bulk action vs single-document action)
- Bulk action success rate (successful completions per document / total documents in bulk action attempts)

### Observable Events (OTEL Instrumentation)
- `documents.search.metadata_query` — metadata search query submitted
- `documents.search.metadata_results` — results returned; result count recorded
- `documents.search.indocument_query` — in-document search triggered
- `documents.tag.applied` — tag applied to document; source: `manual` | `drag_to_smart_view`
- `documents.tag.created` — new tag created by practice admin
- `documents.tag.deleted` — tag deleted by practice admin
- `documents.smartview.generated` — system-generated Smart View created from tag usage
- `documents.smartview.viewed` — Smart View opened; result count recorded
- `documents.bulk.file_initiated` — bulk file action confirmed by user; `document_count`, `eligible_count`, `ineligible_count` recorded as span attributes
- `documents.bulk.file_complete` — bulk file action completed; `success_count`, `failure_count` recorded
- `documents.bulk.code_initiated` — bulk code action confirmed by user; `document_count`, `eligible_count`, `code_count` recorded as span attributes
- `documents.bulk.code_complete` — bulk code action completed; `success_count`, `failure_count` recorded

### Performance SLOs
- Metadata search: p95 < 1 second from query submission to results rendered
- Filter/sort: p95 < 500ms from filter change to list updated
- In-document search: p95 < 500ms for documents up to 50 pages
- Tag application (inline): p95 < 300ms from user action to tag chip appearing on row

### Alerting Conditions

| Condition | Threshold | Severity | Channel |
|---|---|---|---|
| Metadata search latency breach | p95 > 1 second sustained for 5 min | HIGH | Ops alert |
| Bulk action failure spike | > 5% failure rate per bulk action session | HIGH | Ops alert |
| Tag taxonomy cap breach | Practice tag count approaches 80% of configured cap | MEDIUM | Ops alert |
| Filter/sort latency breach | p95 > 500ms sustained for 5 min | MEDIUM | Ops alert |

