### Operations

- Deployment: Progressive delivery by practice cohort and patching domain.
- Monitoring: OTEL traces, SLO dashboards, queue depth and error-rate alerts.
- Logging: Structured logs with ERN identifiers only.
- Runbooks: Incident, rollback, and data-reconciliation procedures required pre-go-live.

### Performance & Cost

- Performance baseline: Maintain p99 user interactions under 2 seconds unless requirement-specific carve-outs apply.
- Scalability baseline: Support baseline and 3x burst workloads with autoscaling.
- Cost approach: Minimise net-new spend by extending existing services first.

### Security

- Authentication and authorisation: JWT scope checks on every API path.
- Encryption: TLS 1.2+ in transit and KMS-backed encryption at rest.
- Network: Private service tiers with ALB ingress and least-privilege security groups.
- Frontend safety: URL value encoding and security headers mandated.

